      "worked": "Yes. His initial translation gives $y=f(x-1)$. Dilate this graph horizontally by a factor of $\\frac32$, replacing $x$ by $\\frac23x$. Then translate left 1 unit, replacing $x$ by $x+1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=f(x-1)\\\\y&=f\\left(\\frac23x-1\\right)\\\\y&=f\\left(\\frac23(x+1)-1\\right)\\\\y&=f\\left(\\frac{2x-1}{3}\\right).\\end{align*}$$\nThe target graph is obtained without reversing his initial step.",
